<title>DUBAI: Iran's NIOC cuts bunker fuel prices from June 5.</title>
<headline>Iran's NIOC cuts bunker fuel prices from June 5.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Iranian Oil Company (NIOC) said on Tuesday it cut 280-cst straight-run fuel oil to $100 a tonne from Kharg Island and $94.50 from Bandar Mahshahr.</p>
<p>The new rates telexed to Reuters by NIOC take effect June 5.</p>
<p>On May 28 NIOC prices stood at $102.50 for ex-Kharg material and $97.50 ex Bandar Mahshahr.</p>
</text>
